      "tag": "p",
    },
    "errors": [],
    "html": "<p class='break-words xs:mb-4'>The coronation of Queen Elizabeth II was the most British of days: a day of glory and spectacle, steeped in tradition and uniting the Commonwealth. And it rained. </p>",
    "id": undefined,
    "properties": undefined,
    "text": "<p class="break-words xs:mb-4">The coronation of Queen Elizabeth II was the most British of days: a day of glory and spectacle, steeped in tradition and uniting the Commonwealth. And it rained. </p>",
    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "component": "body",
    "element": {
      "attributes": {
        "class": "break-words xs:mb-4",
      },
      "tag": "p",
    },
    "errors": [],
    "html": "<p class='break-words xs:mb-4'>The day was 2 June 1953, the new <a href='https://www.discoverbritain.com/history/icons/queen-elizabeth-ii-life-reign-timeline/' target='_blank' class='text-primary underline' aria-label='Queen Elizabeth II'>Queen Elizabeth II</a> had acceded to the throne on 6 February 1952, when her father, King George VI, passed away. The coronation, following a period of mourning and meticulous preparation, marked the occasion. It was to be a day of celebration and solemnity, the centrepiece a ceremony that had remained largely the same for 1,000 years.</p>",
    "id": undefined,
    "properties": undefined,
    "text": "<p class="break-words xs:mb-4">The day was 2 June 1953, the new <a href="https://www.discoverbritain.com/history/icons/queen-elizabeth-ii-life-reign-timeline/" target="_blank" class="text-primary underline">Queen Elizabeth II</a> had acceded to the throne on 6 February 1952, when her father, King George VI, passed away. The coronation, following a period of mourning and meticulous preparation, marked the occasion. It was to be a day of celebration and solemnity, the centrepiece a ceremony that had remained largely the same for 1,000 years.</p>",
    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "component": "body",
    "element": {
      "attributes": {
        "class": "break-words xs:mb-4",
      },
      "tag": "p",
    },
    "errors": [],
    "html": "<p class='break-words xs:mb-4'>There have been 39 coronations held at Westminster Abbey since William the Conqueror’s in 1066, and the bones of the ceremony remain little changed in 1000 years. If you’d like to know more about the ceremony itself, I’d recommend Ian Lloyd’s brilliant <a href='https://amzn.to/4vr0LFa' target='_blank' class='text-primary underline' aria-label='The Throne: 1,000 Years of British Coronations, which is available on Amazon'><i>The Throne: 1,000 Years of British Coronations, </i>which is available on Amazon</a> and details every little bit of history about this ultimate British display of pomp and circumstance. </p>",
    "id": undefined,
    "properties": undefined,
    "text": "<p class="break-words xs:mb-4">There have been 39 coronations held at Westminster Abbey since William the Conqueror’s in 1066, and the bones of the ceremony remain little changed in 1000 years. If you’d like to know more about the ceremony itself, I’d recommend Ian Lloyd’s brilliant <a href="https://amzn.to/4vr0LFa" target="_blank" class="text-primary underline"><i>The Throne: 1,000 Years of British Coronations, </i>which is available on Amazon</a> and details every little bit of history about this ultimate British display of pomp and circumstance. </p>",
    "warnings": [],
  },
