    "errors": [],
    "html": "<p class='break-words xs:mb-4'>The Abbey, the venue of every coronation since 1066, opened at 6 am to about 8,000 guests. Members of the Royal Family, peers and heads of state from across the world glided in after 8.30 am. Then, at 11.15, came the Queen with a procession of 250 people to verses from <i>Psalm 22</i>. </p>",
    "id": undefined,
    "properties": undefined,
