    },
    "errors": [],
    "html": "<h3 class='cmc-header-3 mb-4'>What was so special about Queen Elizabeth II’s Coronation?</h3>",
    "id": undefined,
    "properties": undefined,
    "text": "What was so special about Queen Elizabeth II’s Coronation?",
    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "component": "body",
    "element": {
      "attributes": {
        "class": "break-words xs:mb-4",
      },
      "tag": "p",
    },
    "errors": [],
    "html": "<p class='break-words xs:mb-4'>The Coronation was the first to be televised – and the first event many saw on television. About 27 million people tuned in across the UK, with millions more around the world. About 11 million people tuned in on the radio.</p>",
    "id": undefined,
    "properties": undefined,
    "text": "<p class="break-words xs:mb-4">The Coronation was the first to be televised – and the first event many saw on television. About 27 million people tuned in across the UK, with millions more around the world. About 11 million people tuned in on the radio.</p>",
    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "component": "subtitle",
    "element": {
      "attributes": {
        "class": "cmc-header-3 mb-4",
      },
      "tag": "h3",
    },
    "errors": [],
    "html": "<h3 class='cmc-header-3 mb-4'>What happens at the Coronation of a British monarch?</h3>",
    "id": undefined,
    "properties": undefined,
    "text": "What happens at the Coronation of a British monarch?",
    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "component": "body",
    "element": {
      "attributes": {
        "class": "break-words xs:mb-4",
      },
      "tag": "p",
    },
    "errors": [],
    "html": "<p class='break-words xs:mb-4'>The three-hour service, conducted by the Archbishop of Canterbury, comprised six parts: the Recognition, the Oath, the Anointing, the Investiture (including the Crowning), the Enthronement and the Homage.</p>",
    "id": undefined,
    "properties": undefined,
    "text": "<p class="break-words xs:mb-4">The three-hour service, conducted by the Archbishop of Canterbury, comprised six parts: the Recognition, the Oath, the Anointing, the Investiture (including the Crowning), the Enthronement and the Homage.</p>",
    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "component": "body",
    "element": {
      "attributes": {
        "class": "break-words xs:mb-4",
      },
      "tag": "p",
    },
    "errors": [],
    "html": "<p class='break-words xs:mb-4'>Every object was rich in significance. The Queen was crowned in St Edward’s Chair, made in 1300 for<a href='https://www.discoverbritain.com/history/icons/king-edward-i/' target='_blank' class='text-primary underline' aria-label=' Edward I '> Edward I </a>and used in <a href='https://www.discoverbritain.com/heritage/royals/coronation-ceremonies/' target='_blank' class='text-primary underline' aria-label='every coronation since'>every coronation since</a>. During the ceremony, the Queen was handed the four symbols of authority: the Orb, the Sceptre, the Rod of Mercy and the Sovereign’s Ring. The Orb, a globe of gold surrounded by a cross with diamonds and emeralds, shone in the light. The Ring, also known as The Wedding Ring of England, glittered with sapphire and rubies. </p>",
    "id": undefined,
    "properties": undefined,
    "text": "<p class="break-words xs:mb-4">Every object was rich in significance. The Queen was crowned in St Edward’s Chair, made in 1300 for<a href="https://www.discoverbritain.com/history/icons/king-edward-i/" target="_blank" class="text-primary underline"> Edward I </a>and used in <a href="https://www.discoverbritain.com/heritage/royals/coronation-ceremonies/" target="_blank" class="text-primary underline">every coronation since</a>. During the ceremony, the Queen was handed the four symbols of authority: the Orb, the Sceptre, the Rod of Mercy and the Sovereign’s Ring. The Orb, a globe of gold surrounded by a cross with diamonds and emeralds, shone in the light. The Ring, also known as The Wedding Ring of England, glittered with sapphire and rubies. </p>",
    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "component": "body",
    "element": {
      "attributes": {
        "class": "break-words xs:mb-4",
      },
      "tag": "p",
    },
    "errors": [],
    "html": "<p class='break-words xs:mb-4'>At the moment of coronation, the Archbishop placed the St Edward’s Crown, one of the most iconic symbols of royalty, on the Queen’s head. Dating back to 1661, it is made of solid gold and encrusted with 440 precious and semi-precious stones. A cry of “God save the Queen” went up, and gun salutes were fired as crowds outside cheered.</p>",
    "id": undefined,
    "properties": undefined,
    "text": "<p class="break-words xs:mb-4">At the moment of coronation, the Archbishop placed the St Edward’s Crown, one of the most iconic symbols of royalty, on the Queen’s head. Dating back to 1661, it is made of solid gold and encrusted with 440 precious and semi-precious stones. A cry of “God save the Queen” went up, and gun salutes were fired as crowds outside cheered.</p>",
    "warnings": [],
  },
