        "class": "cmc-header-3 mb-4",
      },
      "tag": "h3",
    },
    "errors": [],
    "html": "<h3 class='cmc-header-3 mb-4'>What happened after Queen Elizabeth II’s Coronation ceremony?</h3>",
    "id": undefined,
    "properties": undefined,
    "text": "What happened after Queen Elizabeth II’s Coronation ceremony?",
    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "component": "body",
    "element": {
      "attributes": {
        "class": "break-words xs:mb-4",
      },
      "tag": "p",
    },
    "errors": [],
    "html": "<p class='break-words xs:mb-4'>The Queen held a coronation luncheon for 11 in the Abbey annex, where she and the Duke of Edinburgh ate smoked salmon, sausage rolls and chicken sandwiches. A banquet was held for guests, many from abroad, in the Great Hall of Westminster School, next door to the Abbey. The star dish was coronation chicken, a recipe created for the occasion. </p>",
    "id": undefined,
    "properties": undefined,
    "text": "<p class="break-words xs:mb-4">The Queen held a coronation luncheon for 11 in the Abbey annex, where she and the Duke of Edinburgh ate smoked salmon, sausage rolls and chicken sandwiches. A banquet was held for guests, many from abroad, in the Great Hall of Westminster School, next door to the Abbey. The star dish was coronation chicken, a recipe created for the occasion. </p>",
    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "component": "body",
    "element": {
      "attributes": {
        "class": "break-words xs:mb-4",
      },
      "tag": "p",
    },
    "errors": [],
    "html": "<p class='break-words xs:mb-4'>For many people outside, the royal procession back from the Abbey to the Palace meant almost as much as the ceremony. At 7.2km, the route was designed to be seen by as many people as possible and took the participants, in their thousands, two hours. The Queen looked resplendent in her Purple Robe of Estate, embroidered with a cipher of the Queen and a border of olive branches and wheat ears, representing peace and plenty.</p>",
    "id": undefined,
    "properties": undefined,
    "text": "<p class="break-words xs:mb-4">For many people outside, the royal procession back from the Abbey to the Palace meant almost as much as the ceremony. At 7.2km, the route was designed to be seen by as many people as possible and took the participants, in their thousands, two hours. The Queen looked resplendent in her Purple Robe of Estate, embroidered with a cipher of the Queen and a border of olive branches and wheat ears, representing peace and plenty.</p>",
    "warnings": [],
  },
