  {
    "component": "body",
    "element": {
      "attributes": {
        "id": "elk-3c89047c-6042-4ae9-8995-b708b08fddaa",
      },
      "tag": "p",
    },
    "errors": [],
    "html": "<p id='elk-3c89047c-6042-4ae9-8995-b708b08fddaa'>It’s fair to say that the devices we use around us disconnect us from our surroundings, so Spiegel sees Specs as a “prison break” from the 7-hour-a-day screen habit that has been over 12 years in the making.</p>",
    "id": "elk-3c89047c-6042-4ae9-8995-b708b08fddaa",
    "properties": undefined,
    "text": "<p id="elk-3c89047c-6042-4ae9-8995-b708b08fddaa">It’s fair to say that the devices we use around us disconnect us from our surroundings, so Spiegel sees Specs as a “prison break” from the 7-hour-a-day screen habit that has been over 12 years in the making.</p>",
    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "component": "body",
    "element": {
      "attributes": {},
      "tag": "p",
    },
    "errors": [],
    "html": "<p>“The biggest problem I see today is that people are spending seven or eight hours a day on their computer. We have to change that,” Spiegel commented. He calls it a “single player” experience that is a “disaster for our society” in pulling us away from one another.</p>",
    "id": undefined,
    "properties": undefined,
    "text": "<p>“The biggest problem I see today is that people are spending seven or eight hours a day on their computer. We have to change that,” Spiegel commented. He calls it a “single player” experience that is a “disaster for our society” in pulling us away from one another.</p>",
    "warnings": [],
  },
  {
    "component": "body",
    "element": {
      "attributes": {},
      "tag": "p",
    },
    "errors": [],
    "html": "<p>And it’s this that drove the philosophy that AR is the only human path. “Holding this tiny little screen in your hands was not the future of computers,” Spiegel proclaimed. Neither does he think it’s VR, as he bluntly critiqued this as “insane” and like “wearing a TV on your face.”</p>",
    "id": undefined,
    "properties": undefined,
    "text": "<p>And it’s this that drove the philosophy that AR is the only human path. “Holding this tiny little screen in your hands was not the future of computers,” Spiegel proclaimed. Neither does he think it’s VR, as he bluntly critiqued this as “insane” and like “wearing a TV on your face.”</p>",
    "warnings": [],
  },
